From 1b77c11539eb410c28c86420c3b8063a9f6ffb88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:57:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] rk3326: add the XiFan RF35H device tree

The XiFan RF35H (sold as XF35H too): RK3326, 640x480 MIPI-DSI panel on
the generic-dsi driver, RK817 PMIC, RK915 Wi-Fi, two sticks on one SARADC
channel behind a 4-way mux, a vibration motor on a GPIO.

Derived from the XF35H tree of AURKNIX, with the changes validated on the
RF35H by the lakka-rf35h port (Linux 7.2.7):

- the panel's default mode is the 60.000 Hz one (31.08 MHz, 1000x518);
  AURKNIX's first line is 58.5 Hz
- full CPU and GPU scales, with 520 and 600 MHz for the GPU at the
  voltage of the 560 MHz point (600 MHz is the stock maximum)
- battery capacity and resistance from the stock tree, BOOST at 5.0 V
- the stick LED controller's power line (GPIO2_A1) kept on
- the factory eMMC disabled: the XiFan loader leaves it timing out

Wi-Fi follows the binding of Batocera's rk915 driver (as on the R36
Ultra): a rockchip,rk915 node with the power line and the host-wake
interrupt, no mmc-pwrseq. The gamepad gets an identity of its own,
because the RF35H has no function key and needs Select as hotkey. The
rumble motor needs the rocknix-joypad GPIO support of the next commit.

Built against Linux 7.2.8 with Batocera's RK3326 patches: no warnings
from this file with W=1.

